        GCA — Git Commit Assistant
        ==========================

GCA is a command-line tool that generates high-quality commit messages
from your staged changes using fast AI inference. You stage your files,
run gca, and get a well-written conventional commit in seconds.

It is built for speed. Inference is powered by Cerebras and Groq.


Quick Start
-----------

  1. Install Go 1.25+ and build:

        $ go build -o gca .
        $ mv gca /usr/local/bin/   # or anywhere in your PATH

  2. Configure your provider and API key:

        $ gca config set provider groq
        $ gca config set api-key <your-key>

     Get a free API key at:
       * Groq:     https://console.groq.com
       * Cerebras: https://cloud.cerebras.ai

  3. Stage some changes and run it:

        $ git add -p
        $ gca


How It Works
------------

  GCA reads your staged diff, sends it to the configured AI provider,
  and returns a commit message in Conventional Commits format:

        $ gca

        ----------------------------------
        feat(auth): add email validation

        - Add regex check for email format on login form
        - Return user-friendly error for invalid addresses
        - Add unit tests for edge cases
        ----------------------------------
        Commit? (y/n/e):

  * y — accept the message and commit
  * n — abort, nothing happens
  * e — edit the message in $EDITOR before committing


Flags
-----

        gca                    Interactive mode (default)
        gca -n, --dry-run      Preview the message, don't commit
        gca --no-input         Commit automatically, no prompt (CI)
        gca --json             Output the message as JSON
        gca -p, --provider     Override provider (groq, cerebras)
        gca -m, --model        Override the AI model


Configuration
-------------

  All config lives in ~/.config/gca/config.json. Manage it with:

        gca config set <key> <value>
        gca config get <key>
        gca config list
        gca config path

  Valid keys: provider, api-key, model.

  Environment variables override the config file:

        GCA_PROVIDER       Provider name (groq, cerebras)
        GROQ_API_KEY       API key for Groq
        CEREBRAS_API_KEY   API key for Cerebras

  Precedence: CLI flags > environment variables > config file.


Providers
---------

  GCA supports two providers, chosen for inference speed:

        Provider    Default Model                          Endpoint
        --------    -------------                          --------
        groq        llama-3.3-70b-versatile                api.groq.com
        cerebras    qwen-3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507         api.cerebras.ai

  Both expose OpenAI-compatible APIs. A single client handles both.


Building from Source
--------------------

        $ git clone https://github.com/chrisdadev13/git-commit-assistant.git
        $ cd git-commit-assistant
        $ go build -o gca .


